---
description: Arcane edit markers and sync-conflict avoidance
globs: "**/*.cs,**/*.yml,**/*.yaml,**/*.ftl,**/*.xaml,**/*.toml,**/*.json,**/*.py"
alwaysApply: true
---

For a changed inherited game/resource/config path read [Arcane marker syntax](../../.agents/rules/arcane-edit-markers.md) and [trajectory](../../.agents/rules/fork-trajectory-priority.md) before editing. The canonical rule owns line-count forms, adjacent compatible blocks, usings, authorship and format limits; do not keep a second table here. Instruction/documentation edits do not use gameplay markers.

An actual conflict follows [merge policy](../../.agents/rules/merge-conflict-resolution.md). Markers identify divergence/history, not correctness or whole-file priority; sprite/map conflicts go to the user. Review checks these contracts without authorizing a resolution.
